chanical Analysis, and General Science.", "time_limit": 60, "parts": [{"part_name": "VERBAL ABILITY", "description": "VERBAL ABILITY section evaluating core competencies.", "questions": [{"question_number": 1, "question_text": "Pick out the most effective word(s) from the given words to fill in the blank to make the sentence meaningfully complete. Woman came in with a baby who, she said, a safety pin.", "option_a": "Was just swallowing", "option_b": "swallowed?", "option_c": "Just Swallowed", "option_d": "", "correct_option": "D"}, {"question_number": 2, "question_text": "Which of these words is the odd one out?", "option_a": "Swindle", "option_b": "harass", "option_c": "provoke", "option_d": "annoy", "correct_option": "C"}, {"question_number": 3, "question_text": "In the following questions choose the word which is the exact OPPOSITE of the given words. ENCOURAGE", "option_a": "Dam", "option_b": "Disapprove", "option_c": "Discourage", "option_d": "Warn", "correct_option": "C"}, {"question_number": 4, "question_text": "Each question consist of two words which have a certain relationship to each other followed by four pairs of related words, Select the pair which has the same relationship. LAWYER: COURT", "option_a": "Businessman: market", "option_b": "chemist: laboratory", "option_c": "Laborer: factory", "option_d": "athlete: Olympics.", "correct_option": "A"}, {"question_number": 5, "question_text": "In the following the questions choose the word which best expresses the meaning of the given word. INDICT", "option_a": "Condemn", "option_b": "Reprimand", "option_c": "Accuse", "option_d": "Allege", "correct_option": "C"}, {"question_number": 6, "question_text": "I felt the wall of the tunnel shiver. The master alarm squealed through my earphones. Almost simultaneously, Jack yelled down to me that there was a warning light on. Fleeting but spectacular sights snapped into an out of view, the snow, the shower of debris, the moon, looming close and big, the dazzling sunshine for once unfiltered by layers of air. The last twelve hours before re-entry were particular bone-chilling. During this period, I had to go up in to command module. Even after the fiery re-entry splashing down in 81o water in south pacific, we could still see our frosty breath inside the command module. Which one of the following reasons would one consider as more as possible for the warning lights to be on?", "option_a": "There was a shower of debris.", "option_b": "Jack was yelling.", "option_c": "A catastrophe was imminent", "option_d": "The moon was looming close and big.", "correct_option": "B"}, {"question_number": 7, "question_text": "In the questions below the sentences have been given in Active/Passive voice. From the given alternatives, choose the one which best expresses the given sentence in Passive/Active voice. They have built a perfect dam across the river.", "option_a": "Across the river a perfect dam was built.", "option_b": "A perfect dam has been built by them across the river.", "option_c": "A perfect dam should have been built by them.", "option_d": "Across the river was a perfect dam.", "correct_option": "A"}, {"question_number": 8, "question_text": "Rearrange the following five sentences in proper sequence so as to for a meaningful paragraph, then answer the questions given below them.", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "2", "option_c": "3", "option_d": "4", "correct_option": "C"}, {"question_number": 9, "question_text": "Which word means - to accumulate; to gather", "option_a": "Abjure", "option_b": "assess", "option_c": "amass", "option_d": "acquire", "correct_option": "B"}, {"question_number": 10, "question_text": "Each question consist of two words which have a certain relationship to each other followed by four pairs of related words, Select the pair which has the same relationship. FISH: SHOAL", "option_a": "audience:theatre", "option_b": "elephant: flock", "option_c": "whale: herd", "option_d": "shark: school", "correct_option": "D"}]}, {"part_name": "NUMERICAL ABILITY", "description": "NUMERICAL ABILITY section evaluating core competencies.", "questions": [{"question_number": 1, "question_text": "The cost price of 20 articles is the same as the selling price of x articles. If the profit is 25%, then the value of x is:", "option_a": "15", "option_b": "16", "option_c": "18", "option_d": "25", "correct_option": "B"}, {"question_number": 2, "question_text": "In the first 10 overs of a cricket game, the run rate was only 3.2. What should be the run rate in the remaining 40 overs to reach the target of 282 runs?", "option_a": "6.25", "option_b": "6.5", "option_c": "6.75", "option_d": "7", "correct_option": "A"}, {"question_number": 3, "question_text": "The cube root of .000216 is:", "option_a": "0.6", "option_b": "0.06", "option_c": "77", "option_d": "87", "correct_option": "A"}, {"question_number": 4, "question_text": "A sum of money at simple interest amounts to Rs. 815 in 3 years and to Rs. 854 in 4 years. The sum is:", "option_a": "Rs. 650", "option_b": "Rs. 690", "option_c": "Rs. 698", "option_d": "Rs. 700", "correct_option": "B"}, {"question_number": 5, "question_text": "A fruit seller had some apples. He sells 40% apples and still has 420 apples. Originally, he had:", "option_a": "588 apples", "option_b": "600 Apples", "option_c": "672 Apples", "option_d": "700 Apples.", "correct_option": "C"}, {"question_number": 6, "question_text": "A clock is started at noon. By 10 minutes past 5, the hour hand has turned through:", "option_a": "145 0", "option_b": "150 0", "option_c": "155 0", "option_d": "160 0", "correct_option": "D"}, {"question_number": 7, "question_text": "A hall is 15 m long and 12 m broad. If the sum of the areas of the floor and the ceiling is equal to the sum of the areas of four walls, the volume of the hall is:", "option_a": "720", "option_b": "900", "option_c": "1200", "option_d": "1800", "correct_option": "C"}, {"question_number": 8, "question_text": "If one-third of one-fourth 